    "title": "Space Florida and Okaloosa Schools announce partnership - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Aubrey Moran ,\n56 minutes ago\nOKALOOSA COUNTY, Fla. ( WKRG ) — The Okaloosa County School District and Space Florida are set to partner to provide students with opportunities in the aerospace industry.\nThere will be a formal announcement during the ninth annual Technology Coast Manufacturing and Engineering Network Industry Day to celebrate the partnership.\nMobile man found guilty in rape cold case from 1997 The announcement will take place on Wednesday, May 13, at the Destin-Fort Walton Beach Convention Center.\nPresident and CEO of Space Florida, Rob Long, is set to give remarks on the future of aerospace and its development in the region.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKRG News 5.",
    "summary": "OKALOOSA COUNTY, Fla. ( WKRG ) — The Okaloosa County School District and Space Florida are set to partner to provide students with opportunities in the aerospace industry. There will be a formal announcement during the ninth annual Technology Coast Manufacturing and Engineering Network Industry Day to celebrate the partnership. Mobile man found guilty in rape cold case from 1997 The announcement will take place on Wednesday, May 13, at the Destin-Fort Walton Beach Convention Center. President and CEO of Space Florida, Rob Long, is set to give remarks on the future of aerospace and its development in the region.",
